# Sinden light guns (#575): the console reads each gun's two input devices
# itself (frontend/src/lightgun.cpp), so nothing else may. libinput, under
# gamescope, would make the gun's absolute mouse a pointer and its keyboard's
# arrow keys player 1's D-pad in every game; SDL would seat a gun in Sinden's
# joystick mode as a player's pad. Told by the USB product string the guns
# carry, "SindenLightgun" (read on the reference console, 2026-11-27), never
# by an id: two guns can share one.
#
# The seat's user gets read access, as systemd gives a pad: a mouse is the
# input group's alone by default. After 60-input-id.rules, which sets
# ID_INPUT_*, and 70-uaccess.rules; before 73-seat-late.rules, which turns the
# tag into the grant. The gun's serial port and camera, which Sinden's own
# software drives, are not matched here.
SUBSYSTEM=="input", ATTRS{product}=="SindenLightgun", ENV{LIBINPUT_IGNORE_DEVICE}="1", \
  ENV{ID_INPUT_JOYSTICK}="", TAG+="uaccess"
